@startuml
title Sequence diagram

actor User
participant "Engagement" as Engagement #purple
participant "Party Interaction" as PartyInteraction #red
participant "Product Configurator" as ProductConfigurator
participant "Recommendation" as Recommendation
participant "Product Catalog" as ProductCatalog
participant "Product Inventory" as ProductInventory

== USER SETS ELIGIBILITY PARAMETETRS, VIEWS ELIGIBLE AND RECOMMENDED OFFERINGS WITH PRICES ==

User -> Engagement : 20. Choose\n"Select Main Offer to Configure"
Engagement -> ProductCatalog : 21. **TMF620 Product Catalog**\nGET /productCategory
activate ProductCatalog
ProductCatalog --> Engagement : 22. 200 OK\nlist of productCategory\n//B2B_offerings among the list//
deactivate ProductCatalog

note over Engagement : select B2B catgogy\nas customer is B2B

Engagement -> Engagement : 23. Display Quote Welcome,\nRequest Country, Regions
Engagement --> User : 24. Present data

User -> Engagement : 25. Selected Country, Regions

alt Present Only Eligible Offerings

    Engagement -> ProductConfigurator : 26. **TMF679 Product Offering Qualification**\nPOST /queryProductOfferingQualification\n(Place=Country, List of Regions,channel="B2B eCommerce Portal",\ncategory=B2B_offerings,\nrelatedParty(id,name="Alice&Bob",role="B2B Customer")
    activate ProductConfigurator

    ProductConfigurator -> ProductCatalog : 27. **TMF620 Product Catalog Mgt**\nGET\n/productOffering?place=[country,region]&channel="B2B eCommerce Portal"&category="B2B_offerings"
    activate ProductCatalog
    ProductCatalog --> ProductConfigurator : 28. **TMF620** OK\n(filtered by country, regions, channel and categiry eligible offerings,\npolicies/rules applied to ProductOfferings, ProductOfferingPrices:\ne.g.restrict the availability of a product offering due to commercial considerations,\nproduct offering price as condition dependent price)
    deactivate ProductCatalog

    ProductConfigurator -> ProductConfigurator : 29. Filter eligible offerings (SASE Contract is among those offerings),\nCalculate prices

    ProductConfigurator --> Engagement : 30. **TMF679 Product Offering Qualification**\n200 OK (list of qualifiedProductOfferingItems)\n//SASE Contract is among those offerings//
    deactivate ProductConfigurator

    Engagement -> Engagement : 31. Display Eligible Offerings\n(SASE Contract is among those offerings)
    Engagement --> User : 32. Present Eligible Offerings

else Present Recommended Offerings

    Engagement -> Recommendation : 33. **TMF680 Recommendation**\nPOST /queryProductRecommendation\n(Place=Country, List of Regions,channel="B2B eCommerce Portal",category=B2B_offerings,\nrelatedParty(id,name="Alice&Bob",role="B2B Customer")
    activate Recommendation

    Recommendation -> ProductCatalog : 34. **TMF620 Product Catalog Mgt**\nGET\n/productOffering?place=[country,region]&\nchannel="B2B eCommerce Portal"&\ncategory="B2B_offerings"
    activate ProductCatalog
    ProductCatalog --> Recommendation : 35. **TMF620** OK\n(filtered by country, regions, channel and categiry eligible offerings,\npolicies/rules applied to ProductOfferings, ProductOfferingPrices:\ne.g.restrict the availability of a product offering\ndue to commercial considerations,\nproduct offering price as condition dependent price)
    deactivate ProductCatalog

    Recommendation -> ProductInventory : 36. **TMF637 Product Inventory**\nGET /product?partyID=AliceBob.id&place=[country,regions]
    activate ProductInventory
    ProductInventory --> Recommendation : 37. **TMF637** 200 OK (list of products (here connectivity products))
    deactivate ProductInventory

    Recommendation -> Recommendation : 38. Build a list of recommendations\n(SASE Contract offering **has Priority 1**)

    Recommendation --> Engagement : 39. **TMF679 Recommendation**\n200 OK (list of recommendationItems)\n//SASE Contract offering **has Priority 1**//
    deactivate Recommendation

    Engagement -> Engagement : 40. Display Recommended Offerings\n(SASE Contract offering is a top offering)
    Engagement --> User : 41. Present Recommended Offerings

end

@enduml
